{
  "dom_id": "step-q102023",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "What is the index of the term $2.56$ for the geometric sequence below?\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=0.4{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=16,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "This geometric sequence is given as a recurrence relation, i.e.,\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=16,\\,r=0.4.\n$$\n\nWe're interested in finding $n$ such that ${a}_{n}=2.56.$ Using the formula for the $n$th term, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\ 2.56 & =16\\cdot {0.4}^{n-1} \\\\ \\frac{2.56}{16} & ={0.4}^{n-1} \\\\ 0.16 & ={0.4}^{n-1} \\\\ {0.4}^{2} & ={0.4}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the exponents gives:\n\n$$\n2=n-1\\,⟹\\,n=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2.56$ is the $3$rd term of the sequence.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
